n AI. I am saying that AI is no reason to stop thinking, and that a model summarising a book is no reason to stop reading it. That would be a mistake.\n\nLearning a language is the clearest example. Speaking it in the street takes skill, memory and constant practice. So keep learning things without AI as a crutch, or the muscles of your brain waste away, and in the end you stop making choices at all: even artistic choices get worse when those muscles go unused. Keep your own way of thinking and your own way of reaching knowledge, through works and books rather than through a model. And works means many things: games, films, books, comics, a podcast on YouTube.\n\nThen use AI as a multiplier, for code and development, because it is excellent at that. Agentic tools like Cursor, Claude Code and ChatGPT are mature enough to build robust programs, and insisting on writing everything by hand would be a mistake. It does require knowing exactly what you are doing, and getting better at it.\n\nWhat matters most is to keep learning alongside AI rather than only with it: think outside the model first, then bring your own thesis to it.\n\nROLE\n\nWhat is my role: Tech Art is a multiplier a bridge for art and code...\n\n...\n\nWhat is my role: Tech Art is a multiplier, a bridge bridging art, especially in 3D, and computer systems automation.\n\nBuild accessible tools for artists, designers, and users.\nCreate reusable systems.\nBoost performance without compromising visuals.\nAvailable for Freelance, Houdini, UE5\nSee more\n\nWhether you're a AAA studio or an indie team, I solve pipeline challenges, build custom tools, and craft environments that tell stories. Every project is an opportunity to push the craft forward through design, tech art, and programming.\n\nI'm looking to collaborate with ambitious, optimistic teams on projects that make an impact.\n\nBreakdown - FLEUR DE LYS\nTrim Sheet Height - FLEUR DE LYS\nPetals Height - FLEUR DE LYS\nCeramic Tiles - Made with Houdini 